# mouse (roadmap os-server.md P12): /dev/mouse, packets as a Microsoft mouse
# sends them (the key script's {mouse}, handed to the driver as IRQ4
# would): moves right and down, left with the left button, far down against
# the screen's edge, then both buttons, which end it. It waits in poll for
# the terminal and the mouse.
program: sh
emulators: bochs mame
install: C /BIN/MOUSE z-mouse.rx
keys: {wait 20}mouse\n{wait 5}{mouse 16 8 -}{wait 2}{mouse -40 0 L}{wait 2}{mouse 127 127 -}{wait 2}{mouse 0 0 LR}
---
rx286, test build
/a$ mouse
Move the mouse; Esc or both buttons end.
x 320, y 100 (column 40, row 12), buttons: none
x 336, y 108 (column 42, row 13), buttons: none
x 296, y 108 (column 37, row 13), buttons: left
x 423, y 199 (column 52, row 24), buttons: none
x 423, y 199 (column 52, row 24), buttons: both
/a$
